-- Regression fixture for issue #920, second half.
--
-- Two DIFFERENT types both spelled `Verdict`, in sibling sections. Nothing is
-- ambiguous here -- section proximity picks Alpha's `Verdict` for the GIVETH
-- and the constructor `no` pins Beta's for the body -- so the type mismatch is
-- entirely genuine, and must still be reported.
--
-- What was broken is only how it READ. `prettyLayout` renders a type from its
-- surface names and never shows uniques, so the message came out as
--
--   must match its type signature at ..., namely
--     Verdict
--   but is here of type
--     Verdict
--
-- which tells the reader nothing at all. The golden must now show each side
-- qualified by where its `Verdict` was declared.

§ Alpha
DECLARE Verdict IS ONE OF yes

§ Beta
DECLARE Verdict IS ONE OF no

§ Alpha
GIVETH A Verdict
t MEANS no
